<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Tooltip @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Tooltip @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview</h1>

<p>
    The Tooltip component provides accessible, hover and focus-triggered supplementary content for a single focusable element, typically an icon-only
    button, or any control whose purpose isn't already conveyed by visible text. It's built on the browser's native Popover API rather than a custom positioned overlay,
    which means the tooltip is promoted to the top layer automatically, positioned relative to its trigger using CSS anchor positioning, and dismissed correctly even
    when it's nested inside other overlays such as dialogs or menus.
</p>

<p>
    Positioning is configurable to any of eight placements around the trigger, with automatic fallback to an alternative position when the preferred one won't fit in
    the viewport. Tooltip content is plain text, including multi-line text where needed. I was kept deliberately simple in line with the WCAG guidance that this component follows, since a tooltip
    is meant to be a brief, glanceable aside rather than a place for interactive or richly formatted content.
</p>

<p>
    <strong>Important: </strong>The Tooltip component uses CSS anchor positioning with fallbacks for when it wont fit in the desired location which was only baseline at the start of the year 2026. 
    Dependant on your target audience and supported browser versions, you may want to consider referencing the OddBird anchor positioning polyfill 
    see: <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" target="_blank" href="https://github.com/oddbird/css-anchor-positioning">https://github.com/oddbird/css-anchor-positioning (opens in new window)</a>
    to support older browser versions.
</p>

